  "result": "I fixed it in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. When a bound was open (`min_open` or `max_open`), the clamped value moved the wrong way, so it landed outside the allowed range.\n\nFor example, `IntRange(0, 10, min_open=True, max_open=True, clamp=True)` returned `-1` for `-5` and `11` for `50`. It now returns `1` and `9`, which I confirmed by running both cases. I didn't run the test suite, and I didn't add a test for the open-bound case.\n\n`FloatRange` doesn't have this problem. It refuses clamping with open bounds.",
